<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Inan Faris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1329">1329</a>–<a href="/years/1358">1358</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinid dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Inan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fari">Faris</a> was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1348 to 1358. He seized power from his father Abu al-Hasan, conquered the Zayyanid kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> in 1352 and briefly took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> in 1357. He built the Bou Inania <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meknes">Meknes</a> and commissioned the account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a>'s travels. He was strangled by his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> in 1358.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-inan-faris.jpg" alt="Abu Inan Faris" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_Inan_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1348 Abu al-Hasan, who had lost Tunisia to the Arab revolt, was deposed by his son <b>Abu Inan Faris</b>, and the Black Death and the rebellions of Tlemcen and Tunis marked the turn; in 1358 Abu Inan was strangled by his own vizier.</blockquote><a href="/empire/marinid-sultanate">Marinid Sultanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Fez, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. Died in Fez, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.04,-5&amp;year=1347" aria-label="Fez on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4423 930 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Abu Inan Faris"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4873 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4873 1200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=34.04,-5&amp;year=1347">What was here in 1347? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
